<title>FRANCE: French health spending up 0.3 pct in April.</title>
<headline>French health spending up 0.3 pct in April.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>French health care spending rose 0.3 percent month-on-month in April and spending over the first four months of 1997 was down 0.1 percent year-on-year, the CNAM national health insurance fund said on Friday.</p>
<p>Non-hospital spending over the first four months of the year was 71.017 billion francs, down 0.9 percent versus the same period a year earlier, showing spending was in line with objectives, a CNAM statement said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
